From ad932310ff1dac16bc278d3abdc8b56d3871e86c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Correa da Silva Sanches <juca@members.fsf.org>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 11:04:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mn10300 dasm: F4 page is two bytes long, not one

disassemble_f4 reads its second opcode byte with opcodes.r8(pc + 1) and
formats it correctly, but returns a length of 1. Every sibling handler on
the F-page (disassemble_f0/f1/f2/f3/f5/f6, same shape, same single
postbyte) returns 2; F4 is the odd one out, and the operands it prints
prove it consumed the postbyte.

The consequence is that a linear disassembly desynchronises after every
F4 instruction: the postbyte is re-read as an opcode and one real
instruction turns into two or three phantom ones. Concretely, on the
Technics SX-KN7000 main-CPU firmware at 0x484357C7 the bytes

    f4 02  fa c8 f5 00  c8 07

are `movbu (d0, a2), d0` + `cmp 0xf5, d0` + `beq`, but come out as

    484357c7: f4        movbu   (d0, a2), d0
    484357c8: 02 fa c8  movbu   d0, (0xc8fa)
    484357cb: f5 00     udf20   d0, d0
    484357cd: c8 07     beq     0x484357d4

- two invented instructions before the stream happens to resynchronise.
There are 3,440 F4 instructions in that ROM's main code region alone,
so the damage to any whole-image listing is substantial, and the same misalignment affects
the debugger's disassembly window whenever it starts scrolling from a
point above an F4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/devices/cpu/mn10300/mn103dasm.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/devices/cpu/mn10300/mn103dasm.cpp b/src/devices/cpu/mn10300/mn103dasm.cpp
index dd5cef3..ca54bb4 100644
--- a/src/devices/cpu/mn10300/mn103dasm.cpp
+++ b/src/devices/cpu/mn10300/mn103dasm.cpp
@@ -339,7 +339,7 @@ offs_t mn10300_disassembler::disassemble_f4(std::ostream &stream, offs_t pc, con
 		util::stream_format(stream, "d%d, (d%d, a%d)", BIT(op2, 4, 2), BIT(op2, 2, 2), BIT(op2, 0, 2));
 	else
 		util::stream_format(stream, "(d%d, a%d), d%d", BIT(op2, 2, 2), BIT(op2, 0, 2), BIT(op2, 4, 2));
-	return 1 | SUPPORTED;
+	return 2 | SUPPORTED;
 }
 
 offs_t mn10300_disassembler::disassemble_f5(std::ostream &stream, offs_t pc, const mn10300_disassembler::data_buffer &opcodes) const
